<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Madara</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Madara is a village and archaeological site near Shumen in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a>. Its cliffs hold the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madara-rider">Madara Rider</a> relief and Greek inscriptions of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgars">Bulgar</a> khans, and the area was an important pagan sanctuary and fortified place of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-bulgarian-empire">First Bulgarian Empire</a>, close to its capitals <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pliska">Pliska</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/preslav">Preslav</a>.</p></div>
